  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "For all integers \\(n \\ge 9,\\) the value of\n\n\\[\\frac{(n + 2)! - (n + 1)!}{n!}\\]\n\nis always which of the following?",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "a multiple of \\(4\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "a multiple of \\(10\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "a prime number"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "a perfect square"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "a perfect cube"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "d",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12b-2020-p6.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Factor \\((n + 1)!\\) from the numerator: \\[ \\begin{gathered} (n + 2)! - (n + 1)! \\\\ {}= (n + 1)!\\,\\big[(n + 2) - 1\\big] \\\\ {}= (n + 1)!\\,(n + 1). \\end{gathered} \\]\n\nDividing by \\(n!\\) leaves \\(\\dfrac{(n + 1)!\\,(n + 1)}{n!}\\) \\(= (n + 1)(n + 1)\\) \\(= (n + 1)^2,\\) which is always a perfect square.\n\nThus, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "Factor \\((n + 1)!\\) out of the numerator",
        "\\((n + 2)! - (n + 1)!\\) \\(= (n + 1)!\\,\\big[(n + 2) - 1\\big]\\) \\(= (n + 1)!\\,(n + 1)\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
